WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.832
JAMIE: Right? Either Microsoft is
genuinely worried, or they read the
political weather

00:00:02.832 --> 00:00:05.664
JAMIE: and decided a self-authored code
looks better than a regulation they
can't

00:00:05.664 --> 00:00:08.496
JAMIE: author.

00:00:08.596 --> 00:00:11.557
RUFUS: Those options are not mutually
exclusive, Jamie.

00:00:11.657 --> 00:00:14.470
JAMIE: No, but the motive changes what
the document is worth.

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:18.303
RUFUS: Let me take us to New York for a
moment, because the

00:00:18.303 --> 00:00:22.036
RUFUS: market told us something this
morning. AP reported global shares lower
on

00:00:22.036 --> 00:00:25.769
RUFUS: September 15th after AI stocks
fell on Wall Street. The catalyst, per

00:00:25.769 --> 00:00:29.502
RUFUS: AP, was Sam Altman and other
industry leaders publicly floating the
idea

00:00:29.502 --> 00:00:33.235
RUFUS: of slowing AI development.

00:00:33.335 --> 00:00:37.882
ALEX: Industry leaders calling for a
slowdown moved markets. That's the
sentence.
